# The artifact must be byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default, so a Windows
# checkout's sources differ from a macOS or Linux one — every byte of every
# text file. The build copies the checked-out files into the bundle, so the
# **tarball** differed too: the same commit produced a different artifact
# hash on Windows.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text, and `eol=lf` says every text
# file is checked out with LF. Binaries are untouched. The artifact's hash
# is the candidate's identity, and an identity that depends on the platform
# it was built on is not an identity.
#
# The file is part of the source digest, so the candidate records that the
# policy is in force rather than assuming it.
* text=auto eol=lf
